    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.99.28: images with a missing condition are left out of the unadjusted test\n\nThe core's excess_test() split image rows with `group == 0 ? g0 : g1`, so a row with a missing condition (R's\nNA_integer_, Python's -1) was counted in the second condition: the unadjusted test (no adjustment, or the unadjusted_*\ncolumns) included those images, while the adjusted design (pair_design_test's keep, .cell_design's keep) left them\nout. split_groups() now skips negative groups, which fixes excess_test() and excess_tau2() for both front ends (one\nchange in the shared core). availability_test() leaves those rows out too. With more than two conditions,\n.cell_pair_test_levels() built Zg from NA groups, so every pair failed (\"no pair could be tested\"); it now fits the\nunadjusted design on the rows with a condition. informative_units() and no_variation already skipped negative groups.\nR encodes a missing condition as NA_integer_ (match() - 1L), which reaches the core as INT_MIN, a negative group.\n\nThe adjusted test is unchanged except where its tau2 is held at the unadjusted value (an added column that varies\nwithin patients, e.g. adjustAbundance with several images per patient). The pooled steps that use every image, the\nallocation side and tau2_image, are not changed.\n\nChecks: refs.R 26 of 26, maxt_refs.R 11 of 11 and memref identical() to 1.99.27 (none has a missing condition).\nMissing-condition cases (scratch/missing_cond_dev/mc_refs.R): with one image per patient the results now equal those\nwith the images removed; R and Python agree to <= 6e-13. testthat: 357 passed, 0 failed (the three new tests fail on\n1.99.27). R CMD check: only the src/concaveman.hpp warning.\n\nCloses #83\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TfsjwkbDbHkX4kJZNe4ER4\n",
    "time": 1792180525
  },
